### 3.2 The canonical cyclic source

On the canonical source, `x=0` is the retained copy of `Phi`.  The same
argument gives

```text
c_0(H)=x*S(x,y),             gcd(x,S)=1,                (3.4)
r o f_mu=c^(-1)S(x,y)^mu.                               (3.5)
